WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:08.039
A cryptographically secure, on-chain list of two hundred and eighty million verified supporters is not an "analogy" or a

2
00:00:08.039 --> 00:00:13.140
"metaphor" or a "nice idea.". It is the largest political mandate in human history.

3
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.480
Nothing else comes close. Politicians can ignore protests. They can ignore polls.

4
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.320
They can ignore reality for surprisingly long periods (see: climate change, nineteen seventy to present).

5
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:33.820
They cannot ignore two hundred and eighty million cryptographically verified humans saying "do this thing or we vote you

6
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.700
out.". Here's how to build that list. What You're Actually Building.

7
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.920
The Goal. Build a privacy-preserving, globally verifiable referendum.

8
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:49.140
It shows public support for a one percent treaty and Decentralized Institutes of Health.

9
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:56.820
Essentially, a website where people say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" in a way that lawyers find convincing.

10
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:03.460
Requirements: Must be auditable (so politicians can't claim it's fake, though they will absolutely try).

11
00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:08.700
Must be persuasive (so policymakers actually do their jobs for once).

12
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:16.340
Must hit three point five percent global participation (more than two hundred and eighty million verified votes).

13
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:23.900
That last number isn't arbitrary. Once three point five percent of a population actively supports something, it becomes

14
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.960
unstoppable. Every time. Across all cultures. For centuries.

15
00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:37.860
More on that later. The Principles (Or: How Not to Build a Fraudulent Voting System): Cryptographic proofs that votes are

16
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:44.220
real (can't fake the math, though politicians will try). Nobody knows who you voted for (including us).

17
00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.600
Works for everyone, including people without bank accounts or government I.D.s (which is most of Earth, by the way).

18
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:58.940
Open-source code so anyone can audit it. Needs to spread organically with a viral growth target of one point zero (each

19
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.770
person brings more than one person, which is how avalanches work).

20
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:09.060
Greater than ninety-nine percent fraud detection with less than one percent false positives (the bots stay out, the humans

21
00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:16.500
stay in). Secondary metrics track geographic distribution, brand awareness, and whether politicians have started sweating

22
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.440
yet. (The sweat metric is informal but surprisingly reliable.

23
00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:28.680
They always sweat before they act.). The Bottom Line. Two hundred and fifty million dollars for the campaign, funded by

24
00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:34.660
VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds. Target cost: less than one dollar per verified participant.

25
00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.180
That's cheaper than acquiring a customer for literally any consumer product on Earth.

26
00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:47.780
You spend more marketing soda. Two hundred and eighty million verified humans saying "do this or lose your job" to every

27
00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:52.220
politician on Earth. That's not a petition. Petitions are what you ignore.

28
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.300
That's a pink slip with two hundred and eighty million signatures.

29
00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:04.340
On Why three point five percent Is The Magic Number. The two hundred and eighty million target isn't pulled from thin air.

30
00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:11.800
It's based on the "three point five percent Rule," a historical pattern that has held across cultures, centuries, and continents

31
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:20.580
with the reliability of a physical law: When three point five percent of a population actively participates in sustained,

32
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:28.160
nonviolent action, the movement wins. Every time. The evidence: The Civil Rights movement in the U.S.

33
00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.040
crossed the three point five percent threshold and ended segregation.

34
00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.500
Indian Independence crossed the three point five percent threshold and kicked out the British Empire.

35
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:42.920
Women's Suffrage crossed the three point five percent threshold and won the vote.

36
00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:51.620
Once you hit three point five percent, three things happen simultaneously: it's clearly not a fringe movement, the support

37
00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.960
